window.docContents[24].resolve({"/Categorical-tactics-for-kernels/#Kernel-Hom___-Tactics-for-Kernel-Categorical-Reasoning--Categorical-tactics-for-kernels":{"contents":"Two of the most powerful tactics for categories in Mathlib are monoidal and coherence. To facilitate the use of these tactics for kernel equalities, Kernel-Hom provides the kernel_disch, kernel_monoidal, kernel_coherence and aesop_kernel tactics which first apply kernel_hom to the goal to translate the kernel equality into a categorical equality in the SFinKer category, then apply, respectively, monoidal and cat_disch, monoidal, coherence, or aesop (with the CategoryTheory rule set) to solve or simplify the categorical equality. kernel_disch is the tactic to use by default: it tries both monoidal and cat_disch, each after normalizing the tensor products of morphisms, which allows it to use the exchange law, the coassociativity of copy and the comonoid laws of copy and discard, including for deterministic and Markov kernels.\n\nThe kernel_disch tactic applies the kernel_hom transformation to the goal and then\ntries to solve the resulting goal with:1. monoidal, after simp together with the splitting of the tensor products of compositions and\nthe coassociativity of the comultiplication;2. cat_disch, after merging the whiskers and the compositions of tensor products into single\ntensor products, together with the counit and comultiplication laws of the comonoid structure\nand of the deterministic and Markov kernels. This handles the exchange law and the laws hidden in\ntensor products.As it tries both cat_disch and monoidal, it is the tactic to use by default.\n\nThe kernel_monoidal tactic applies the kernel_hom transformation to the goal and then\ninvokes the monoidal tactic to solve or simplify the resulting goal.\n\nThe kernel_coherence tactic applies the kernel_hom transformation to the goal and then\ninvokes the coherence tactic to solve the resulting goal.\n\nThe aesop_kernel tactic applies the kernel_hom transformation to the goal and then\ninvokes aesop with the CategoryTheory rule set, using the same configuration as aesop_cat.\n\nFor more details on the implementation of the monoidal and coherence tactics, see the documentation made by @Yuma Mizuno.\n\n\n","context":"Kernel-Hom: Tactics for Kernel Categorical Reasoning","header":"6. Categorical tactics for kernels","id":"/Categorical-tactics-for-kernels/#Kernel-Hom___-Tactics-for-Kernel-Categorical-Reasoning--Categorical-tactics-for-kernels"}});